      "seed": 849455539,
      "version": 1175,
      "versionNonce": 903861405,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789909359401,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Think about the problem before the solution:\n - The complexity of a problem for an AI to solve is\ndetermined by the level of certainly on the steps it has to\ntake to solve it.\nExamples:\n    - A transcriptions system: take the transcription, analyse\nit, there are some metrics we must analyse, only a call is\nneeded, if there is something to calculate, THERE IS, no\ndecission of how to do it is needed, no decission on if it\nshould be done is needed, no agentic runtime is needed.\n    - An automatic research system: does it have the answer\nin its training? Will it need to go to the internet for\nrefreshing data? Will it need to do the search one time? two\ndifferent searches for different topics? Then compare them?\n\n    - \n\n    \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Think about the problem before the solution:\n - The complexity of a problem for an AI to solve is determined by the level of certainly on the steps it has to take to solve it.\nExamples:\n    - A transcriptions system: take the transcription, analyse it, there are some metrics we must analyse, only a call is needed, if there is something to calculate, THERE IS, no decission of how to do it is needed, no decission on if it should be done is needed, no agentic runtime is needed.\n    - An automatic research system: does it have the answer in its training? Will it need to go to the internet for refreshing data? Will it need to do the search one time? two different searches for different topics? Then compare them?\n\n    - \n\n    \n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
